<div class="card"><h2>Channel utilization</h2>{chan_bars_html}
<h2 style="margin-top:12px">Signal ranking (top 12)</h2>{sig_bars_html}</div>
<div class="card"><h2>Band &amp; security breakdown</h2><div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:16px">
<div><h3>Bands</h3><table>{band_rows_html}</table></div>
<div><h3>Security</h3><table>{sec_rows_html}</table></div></div>
<p class="muted">WPA1/TKIP and WEP are deprecated. WPA2 (CCMP) is the baseline; WPA2/WPA3-transitional or WPA3-SAE preferred.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h2>Signal history (7 days)</h2>{hist_svg}
<h3>Recent link snapshots</h3><table><tr><th>Time</th><th>SSID</th><th>Signal</th><th>GW ping</th><th>Inet ping</th></tr>{link_rows_html}</table></div>
<div class="card"><h2>Bandwidth workload — 24h / 7 days</h2>{bw_kpis}
<h3>Traffic per hour (last 24h, bytes)</h3>{bw_bars_24}
<h3>Traffic per day (last 7 days, bytes)</h3>{bw_bars_7d}
<h3>Workload distribution vs normal (hourly combined rate)</h3>{bw_gauss}
<p class="muted">Gray bars: observed hourly rates. Black curve: fitted normal N(μ, σ²). Bars hugging the curve ≈ steady workload; heavy right tail = burst-heavy usage. Counters sample on every scan/info/report — add <code>nwpcs-wlandiag bw sample</code> to cron for denser history.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h2>Channel advisor</h2>{advisor_html}<p class="muted">Scores weigh nearby APs by signal strength — 2.4 GHz accounts for channel overlap, 5 GHz for co-channel sharing. Apply the pick on your router, then re-scan.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h2>Security audit</h2><ul class="recs">{audit_html}</ul></div>
<div class="card"><h2>Repair kit (works offline)</h2>
<p class="muted">Every fix below ships inside the tool — run <code>nwpcs-wlandiag fix</code> to apply them guided (diagnose → confirm → repair → verify), or copy-paste manually with no internet. ● marks rows matching this run's symptoms.</p>
<table><tr><th>When</th><th>Fix</th></tr>{kit_html}</table></div>
<div class="card"><h2>Throughput</h2>{speed_html}</div>
<div class="card"><h2>Connectivity diagnostics</h2>
<table><tr><th>Target</th><th>Loss</th><th>min</th><th>avg</th><th>max</th><th>mdev</th></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">gateway {esc(data["gw"])}</td><td class="mono">{esc(pg["loss"])}</td><td class="mono">{esc(pg["min"])} ms</td><td class="mono"><strong>{esc(pg["avg"])} ms</strong></td><td class="mono">{esc(pg["max"])} ms</td><td class="mono">{esc(pg["mdev"])} ms</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">8.8.8.8 (internet)</td><td class="mono">{esc(pe["loss"])}</td><td class="mono">{esc(pe["min"])} ms</td><td class="mono"><strong>{esc(pe["avg"])} ms</strong></td><td class="mono">{esc(pe["max"])} ms</td><td class="mono">{esc(pe["mdev"])} ms</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">google.com (DNS+inet)</td><td class="mono">{esc(pd["loss"])}</td><td class="mono">{esc(pd["min"])} ms</td><td class="mono"><strong>{esc(pd["avg"])} ms</strong></td><td class="mono">{esc(pd["max"])} ms</td><td class="mono">{esc(pd["mdev"])} ms</td></tr></table>
<h3>DNS</h3><pre>{esc(data["resolvectl"] or data["dns_conf"])}</pre>
<h3>Active connections</h3><pre>{esc(data["conn_active"])}</pre>
</div>
<div class="card"><h2>Event log — NetworkManager (last {log_minutes} min)</h2><pre>{log_html}</pre></div>
<div class="card"><h2>How this was collected (Linux ≈ netsh wlanreport)</h2>
<pre>nmcli device wifi rescan && nmcli -t -f IN-USE,SSID,BSSID,MODE,CHAN,FREQ,RATE,SIGNAL,BARS,SECURITY device wifi list --rescan yes
nmcli -f GENERAL,IP4,IP6,DHCP4 device show {esc(iface)}
iw dev {esc(iface)} link; iw dev {esc(iface)} station dump
ip route show; resolvectl status {esc(iface)}
ping -c 5 &lt;gateway&gt;; ping -c 5 8.8.8.8; ping -c 5 google.com
journalctl -u NetworkManager --since "{log_minutes} min ago"</pre>
<p class="muted">Windows: <code>netsh wlan show networks mode=bssid</code> then <code>netsh wlanreport</code>.</p></div>
</div>
<footer>Generated by nwpcs-wlandiag v{VERSION} · {esc(now_local.isoformat())} · open this file in any browser (file://) — no server needed.</footer>
